    "narrative": "LawDog enters today\u2019s slate with **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Taylor Ward** headlining our optimal lineup, both boasting scores of 66.5. **Geraldo Perdomo** is a primary target against Marquez due to a favorable 5.64 xERA matchup, providing a 19% SP skill boost that elevates his floor significantly. Meanwhile, **Taylor Ward** is leveraged in the leadoff spot against Boyd; his score is propped up by a 16% park factor and a 9% platoon advantage, though he carries the highest volatility of the day due to a 45% rain risk. We are also capitalizing on high-ceiling matchups with **Gavin Sheets**, who benefits from a 4.98 xERA matchup against Gallen, and **Tyler Freeman**, whose value is bolstered by a favorable steal environment against a pitcher with a slow delivery, reinforcing our commitment to maximizing SB opportunities across the board.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Dylan Beavers**, who remained the odd man out with a score of 44.0. While **Dylan Beavers** carries the same park and weather profile as **Taylor Ward**, his lower-order placement (8th) and a detrimental platoon disadvantage against Boyd suppressed his efficiency compared to our starters. Elsewhere, we continue to monitor the status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who remains sidelined on the IL; his absence remains the primary drag on our offensive output. We are also keeping a close watch on **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Luis Arraez**; despite their moderate scores, they are facing Miles (3.12 xERA) and will need to rely on the wind-out conditions at the park to maintain their viability. With **Jonathan Aranda**, **Bryson Stott**, **Masyn Winn**, **Daulton Varsho**, and **Cal Raleigh** rounding out the lineup, we are well-positioned to balance plate discipline against the day's pitching threats.",
